  "body": "Closes #6469\n\n## What\n\n`SignedReplicationEnvelope::sign` now refuses every envelope that fails an envelope-local rule `ReplicationTracker::accept` enforces, instead of only refusing a wrong-source key and an over-bound payload:\n\n- unsupported envelope version\n- journal header version outside `JOURNAL_VERSION..=MAX_JOURNAL_VERSION`\n- payload digest not equal to `payload_digest(payload)`\n- payload not chaining to `cursor_after` (including malformed / undecodable payload)\n- snapshot whose `cursor_before` is not the chain base for its world/source/header version\n- terminal with a non-empty payload or `cursor_before != cursor_after`\n- snapshot/tail payload whose journal header disagrees with the envelope (#4486 rule)\n\nThe checks live in a new `validate_envelope_local` helper that returns the same `ReplicationError` `accept` would name; `sign` maps any error to `None`. Receiver-state rules (world/pinned source, session nonce, `prev_frame_digest`, tail cursor position / snapshot version vs. the tracker's current chain) stay receiver-only, as the issue scopes them. The `sign()` doc comment now states the full refusal contract.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New `sign_refuses_envelopes_every_receiver_would_reject` pins all eight refused shapes from the issue at the signer, with a valid-constructor control that still signs `Some` and is accepted by a fresh tracker.\n- Existing receiver tests that intentionally sign lying envelopes now build them through bypass helpers (`sign_bypass` in `replication::tests`, the existing `sign_unbounded` in `replication_receiver::tests`), per the acceptance criteria — never through the production `sign()`.\n- `cargo test --manifest-path pkgs/id/Cargo.toml --lib replication`: 47 passed.\n- Full `id` lib suite: 2505 passed + 332 passed, 0 failed (laptop, 2026-11-09).\n\nOracle: `ReplicationTracker::accept`'s envelope-local refusals — a frame the production signer produces must never be one every receiver rejects on envelope-local grounds.\n",
